                <pb facs="0484" n="386" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg386"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/156: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-17T11:00:00-03:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 17,
                                1920—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:15
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>124. Department’s December 9, 2 p.m. After consulting President, Foreign Minister
                    informed me yesterday Brazilian Government is in accord with the decision of the
                    American Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
